A record \(\rho\) is carried by a system \(S\) under scope \(\mathcal C\) if:
\begin{enumerate}
  \item \(\rho\) is a coordinate of the carrier state rather than an analyst
  annotation;
  \item its updates occur in the support of \(S\)'s transition kernel; and
  \item the accepting source record is generated by \(S\)'s trajectory under
  the declared scope, never by fallback or an off-kernel edit.
\end{enumerate}
A carried instrument is an instrument whose visibility, thresholds, and
check-rule records all satisfy these conditions.

