expanded_source_wording_tex:
\label{def:d4-repair-step}
For pre-state \(z\), post-state \(z'\), defect record \(d\), generated move
\(m=\mathfrak R_S(d)\), and audit record \(a\), a lawful repair step requires:
\begin{enumerate}
  \item carried evidence for \(d\), \(m\), and \(a\);
  \item detection of \(d\) by the active carried instrument;
  \item instrument permission for the move's repair sort;
  \item membership of the charged budget line in the complete carried
  ledger;
  \item admissibility of the move at \(z\);
  \item realization \(K(z,z')>0\) in the carrier kernel; and
  \item a successful carried re-audit at \(z'\).
\end{enumerate}
The repair sorts are the P1--P5 roles; P6 is the audit surface and is not
itself admitted as a repair sort.

