expanded_source_wording_tex:
\label{thm:e7}
Under a same-claim, branch-valid, kind-unique disposition package, a
viability-coupled positive-excess witness has exactly one lawful
disposition: (i) currentization by a carried preemptive exposure rewrite;
(ii) statused boundary nonclosure when the viability probe fails to descend;
or (iii) lawful discount when audit shows artifact, currentizability,
out-of-horizon scope, or dissolved coupling.  Currentization is an alarm only
when the constraint set changes; winning inside the old E6 policy is ordinary
attention.

